From 5aaa549fe5e82b4362b54cb7b9d0e9628bc3b55c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arbion Halili <99731180+ToxicPine@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:22:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] vm_memory: span adjacent regions

Let ordinary guest-memory operations span adjacent regions while keeping
host-pointer and volatile APIs single-region. Preserve short I/O at real
holes and validate complete ranges before destructive operations.
---
 arch/src/lib.rs                         |  29 ++-
 base/src/file_traits.rs                 | 132 ++++++++++-
 kernel_loader/src/arm64.rs              |   7 +-
 kernel_loader/src/lib.rs                |  31 ++-
 kernel_loader/src/multiboot.rs          |  23 +-
 vm_memory/src/guest_memory.rs           | 283 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 vm_memory/src/guest_memory/sys/linux.rs |  78 ++++---
 x86_64/src/bzimage.rs                   |  55 ++++-
 8 files changed, 538 insertions(+), 100 deletions(-)

